\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Finite additivity on residue classes}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{The sum in \ref{fdip-00C3} equates the #{p} finer values
with the coarser value at every coherent sequence. When
#{p} is prime, countable additivity of the ball assignment
is not proved, and these identities do not produce a measure
on the Borel sets of the #{p}-adic integers. Each rescaled
class mean sends a function on one residue ring to a function
on a coarser residue ring. Extending the same sums to the
#{p}-adic numbers would require classes outside the
#{p}-adic integers, and no such maps are defined.}
